    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "This is the integer-specific fact the ordered field RR lacks, and the one an integer-cut / Diophantine refutation invokes to kill a residue g*m = r with 0 < r < g. It was previously the headline ASSUMPTION of the integer route; it is now derived. The proof splits x on its constructor: for `Int.negSucc n` the hypothesis `0 < x` itself reduces to `False`, and for `Int.ofNat n` the two bounds reduce to `1 <= n` and `n+1 <= 1`, which chain through `Nat.le_of_succ_le_succ`, `Nat.le_trans` and `Nat.not_succ_le_zero` to a contradiction. Those three Nat theorems are not themselves in this ledger; all are axiom-free (`nat_axiom_inventory` reports zero trusted declarations for the whole Nat environment). formal.statement is `Kernel::render_lean` of the admitted type, verbatim from `int_theorem_inventory`.",
